# Copy to services/catalog/.env for anything other than the default.
# The file is read by src/env.ts through process.loadEnvFile, and a variable
# already present in the environment always wins, so CI and one-off overrides
# such as `CATALOG_DB=... npm run catalog -- status` are never shadowed.
#
# .gitignore already covers .env* except .env.example. Never commit a real one.

# The catalog database, a SQLite file (docs/SQLITE-MIGRATION.md). Unset, it
# is $GNOSIA_HOME/catalog.db, or ~/.gnosia/catalog.db when GNOSIA_HOME is
# unset, which is what daily development runs against: no server, no
# password, no configuration. CATALOG_DB names another file, as a path or a
# sqlite: URL. DATABASE_URL is read after it when it names a file, which is
# what the tests and scripts that point at a scratch file set; a postgres://
# value in either is refused rather than read as a path (databasePath in
# src/env.ts).
# CATALOG_DB=~/.gnosia/catalog.db

# The submodule checkouts. Each defaults to where .gitmodules puts it, so
# none needs setting; they exist because that location has changed once
# already (the pair moved from the repo root into tools/ on 2026-09-13) and
# because a checkout kept outside the superproject is a reasonable thing to
# have. A relative value resolves against the repo root, not the working
# directory, and a leading ~ is expanded.
#
# MANIMKC_ROOT is manimkc's own variable and means the same thing here: the
# *checkout*, which `catalog index` reads and runs the pinned CLI out of.
# `--manimkc-root` overrides it for one run. It is NOT MANIMKC_HOME, which is
# where manimkc's renders land; the indexers take that from each report's
# `outRoot` and never from a path set here.
# MANIMKC_ROOT=tools/manimkc

# REMOTIONKC_ROOT is the same thing for remotionkc, the second video tool, and
# is remotionkc's own variable too. `--remotionkc-root` overrides it for one
# run. Its renders land under REMOTIONKC_HOME, which this repo never reads:
# the indexer takes it from the report's `outRoot`, as for manimkc.
# REMOTIONKC_ROOT=tools/remotionkc

# REVIDEOKC_ROOT is the same thing for revideokc, the third video tool, and is
# revideokc's own variable too. `--revideokc-root` overrides it for one run.
# Its renders land under REVIDEOKC_HOME, which this repo never reads: the
# indexer takes it from the report's `outRoot`, as for manimkc.
# REVIDEOKC_ROOT=tools/revideokc

# BLENDERKC_ROOT is the same thing for blenderkc, the fourth video tool, and is
# blenderkc's own variable too. `--blenderkc-root` overrides it for one run.
# Its renders land under BLENDERKC_HOME, which this repo never reads: the
# indexer takes it from the report's `outRoot`, as for manimkc.
# BLENDERKC_ROOT=tools/blenderkc

# TLDRAWKC_ROOT is the tldrawkc checkout, whose dist/ build reads the .tldr
# files. `npm run canvas` in the root package.json reads the same variable, so
# the tool and the indexer cannot end up on different builds.
# TLDRAWKC_ROOT=tools/tldrawkc

# The knowledge base's repo root: the directory holding learn/. A test-fixture
# override, not a deployment setting. `learn-cli.test.ts` points it at a
# throwaway tree (with DATABASE_URL at a scratch database file) so a test run cannot
# touch the real learn/ or the real gnosia. Leave it unset and every learn
# command works against this repo.
# LEARN_ROOT=/tmp/learn-fixture

# Let this process write to a database whose catalog_instance row says `copy`
# (edge case 14 of docs/CONTENT-MIGRATION.md). Every table carries a statement
# trigger that refuses writes on a copy and names the primary; this flag makes
# the connection's `catalog_copy_ok()` answer 1, which the trigger lets
# through (src/db.ts).
# For the test suites and scripts/e2e.mjs, which write to throwaway copies on
# purpose. Never set it here: a laptop that needs it is pointed at the wrong
# database. `catalog migrate` sets it by itself, since a copy's schema still
# has to follow the primary's.
# CATALOG_COPY_OK=1

# The data root for the laptop's blob store, which keeps objects under
# $GNOSIA_HOME/blobs (docs/CONTENT-MIGRATION.md 0.4). Defaults to
# ~/.gnosia, so the store is ~/.gnosia/blobs. Absolute or starting
# with ~/; a relative value is refused rather than resolved against wherever a
# command happens to run. `fsStore` refuses a root inside a gnosia
# checkout. `blobRoot()` in src/env.ts reads it, for the catalog CLI and for
# the web app alike, which is why this file is the place to set it. Tests and
# scratch work point it at a temporary directory.
# GNOSIA_HOME=~/.gnosia

# Per-owner caps on the blob store (phase 4 of docs/CONTENT-MIGRATION.md):
# the most bytes one owner's objects may add up to, and the most new objects
# one owner may upload in a rolling 24 hours, both measured from blob_object by
# the key's `<owner_id>/` prefix and checked by every upload of a new object
# before a byte moves (a key that already has a row is never refused). Whole
# numbers; 0 refuses every new upload for every owner. Unset, the
# default, is no cap, which is right while one owner uploads from their own
# laptop. A value that is not a whole number refuses every upload, naming the
# variable, rather than silently dropping the cap. `catalog blob audit` prints
# the caps in force and each owner's totals.
# GNOSIA_OWNER_BYTES_CAP=
# GNOSIA_OWNER_UPLOADS_PER_DAY=
